steps.detail:
Use the matching protocol as well as this one:
- overheated, after exertion or in hot weather: a seizure in the heat can be heat stroke; use the Heat illness (heat stroke, heat exhaustion, cramps) protocol now and start cooling;
- a blow to the head or a fall: use the Head injury and concussion protocol;
- diabetes (CDC lists diabetes with loss of consciousness as a reason to call 911): use the Low blood sugar protocol, which gives sugar only once they are fully awake and can swallow;
- a possible poison, drug or overdose: use the Poisoning (swallowed, inhaled, skin or eye) protocol or the Opioid overdose protocol;
- several people with headache, confusion or nausea in a tent, cabin or vehicle with a stove, heater or engine: use the Carbon monoxide poisoning protocol.
